# Browser
# CR 724.1. What a player sees of a turn ended by an effect: Obeka's question is put to the player whose turn it is in its
# own words - end the turn, what that does to the stack - with neither button the default, and once it is answered the
# game log says whose turn ended and that Bot2's Lightning Bolt was exiled, the stack row is empty, and the next turn is
# Bot2's.
#
# Turn 1: Obeka is cast. Turn 3: Bot2 casts Lightning Bolt at Bot1 in Bot1's main phase; Bot1 taps Obeka in response and,
# asked as the player whose turn it is, ends the turn. The Bolt is exiled and Bot1 stays at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Obeka, Brute Chronologist
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Obeka, Brute Chronologist.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Obeka, Brute Chronologist.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Obeka, Brute Chronologist: end the turn?
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = Every spell and ability on the stack is exiled  ·  the rest of the turn is skipped, straight to cleanup
? Client.Bot1.Dock = End the turn; Don't end it
Bot1.Accept
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Client.Bot1.Log.Has = Your turn ends.
? Client.Bot1.Log.Has = [Lightning Bolt] is exiled.
? Client.Bot1.Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Life = 20
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Obeka, Brute Chronologist.Tapped = true
